  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The dimensions of the quantities are as follows.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace></math></p><p>The dimensional form of stress is same as pressure.</p><p>Torque <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math> Force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo></math> distance<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ML</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />Stress <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>&#160;Force&#160;</mtext><mtext>&#160;Area&#160;</mtext></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />Pressure Gradient <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ML</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mr